{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410795-what-would-a-technocracy-civil-war-mean","id":1410795,"title":"What would a Technocracy civil war mean?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-27T19:34:11-07:00","id":1410795,"title":"What would a Technocracy civil war mean?","content":"The books talk about its possibility, so I\u2019m curious how it might play out. Is there any chance a Tradition Mage could mediate between the groups and earn a permanent cease fire between the factions? Possibly one that includes not brainwashing Orphans they pull off the street?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T22:16:31-07:00","id":1410802,"title":"","content":"Void Explorers and Progenitors secede and join up with the Society of Ether and Virtual Adapts to form their own mad science faction. <br /> <br /> The remaining technocratic conventions go full fascist/nephandic and become the setting's Big Bad.<br /> <br /> As for the traditions...? Perhaps the fall out convinces the Ahl-i-Batin that the Traditions are not under Nephandic control after all and they reclaim the now open seat of Correspondence. Maybe they bring back the Solificati as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T05:21:27-07:00","id":1410833,"title":"","content":"From what I understood it means either the Technocracy is going back to way more human standard or going into dictator mode which end like all dictators with Erdogan in Turkey the best example to see.<br /> <br /> What I mean the main fight will be between Syndicate and NWO about what is the meaning of the Technocracy. Gentle nudging the masses to their own good playing the manager here and there or controlling them until they all share one mind and every disturbing things are eliminated. From my opinion this is a war less won because who has the right opinion but it is like World War I situation for the NWO. You either prevent it and go diplomacy to difuse the bomb on that you sit or you eliminate or scare away the Syndicate who controlls the money. Unless the Iteration-X can pull a Star Trek Replicator out of the bag and can bring the masses to accept it they have lost because they will run out of money then. If they make it to still get the funding from It X, Progenitors and mayby NWO then they are still on the loosing track because Syndicate who will likely ally with VA and Etherites and use their financial power together with the Datacontroll of the VAs to influence the market so much, that the Technocrats will be soon out of money to properly work.<br /> <br /> So the only real future beside replicators for abondoning money would be NWO get kicked out and Syndicate is now doing more or less the controll thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T06:14:54-07:00","id":1410838,"title":"","content":"You have the Hyper capitalist Syndicate on one side whole believe the future of humanity is 1share = 1vote and the hyper fascist NWO who is willing to let you think what ever you want as long as those thoughts are committee approved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T07:57:11-07:00","id":1410849,"title":"","content":"Here. Have this thread from the days of yore, when the Civil War was a novelty. It has very interesting points:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/53067-what-happens-in-a-technocratic-civil-war\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...atic-civil-war</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T13:36:12-07:00","id":1410876,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm going to echo the statements I said in that thread, a modern TCW would not be a clean divide along Convention lines because none of the Conventions are a monolith. It will be a messy divide between beliefs within the Union as a whole.<br /> <br /> As I see it, that divide would likely be between two particular things, either what they want to do with the Mages and Supernaturals, and what they want to do about the state of the Masses right now. Though in either case it would more or less be a fight between Moderates and Conservatives.<br /> <br /> For example, in the Rev Ed CBs, the only people expressing any real desire to return to Pogrom is within the Progenitors basically because they're fed up with the Faith Healers, New Age 'Medicine', the Anti-Vax Movement and other such groups that are causing Sleepers to suffer and die from diseases that can be treated. If there's a split born over what to do about the Supernaturals, those Progenitors will side with whoever pushes for a hardline stance but that may not be the entire Convention as like I said, they're a faction within the Convention and not every Progenitor agrees with them.<br /> <br /> The Void Engineers whom you'd think would jump at the chance to leave the Union or get rid of the Hardliners within it. But they're the ones in the Union that would do everything in their power to stop such a conflict from happening because they <b><i><u>know</u> </i></b>that there are much bigger things to worry about and such a fight would not just endanger the Union but the entire world. And by their own admission, the talk of jumping ship died with the Avatar Storm. They're not leaving the Union and any talk otherwise is either BS to scare the other Conventions to getting what they need or from morons that haven't gotten the memo about the state of the world and the Convention, and how that's a VERY bad idea.<br /> <br /> There is certainly a NWO/Syndicate rivalry within the Union that make people think that they would be the big driving force behind a civil war but honestly looking at it, it's more typical jockey for more power and influence between the two leading Convention. Even by their own admission, while they expect a schism between the two, neither wants it. And let's face it, they've been doing this since the early days of the Order of Reason, when they were the Cabal of Pure Thought and the High Guild respectively.<br /> <br /> Basically they're more bark than bite when it comes to their rivalry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T21:12:53-07:00","id":1410943,"title":"","content":"That is interesting. So many ways it could play out. I remember over a decade ago, when Revised painted the Technocracy as necessary and something the Traditions would have to learn to coexist beside, somebody mentioned that my Hermetic could play the role of Merlin, teaming up with moderate Technocrats (Knights of the Round Table) to protect the Technocracy from splitting up into civil war. <br /> <br /> My main problem with ending the Ascension War was that it left the world doomed, but without any serious way to fight for it. Tastes change, and looking back, I actually like the idea of an uneasy truce between the Traditions and the Technocracy, with the occasional team up. I am also fond of the Spy\u2019s Demise as a potential neutral ground where they can actually talk to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-29-2020, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T09:21:27-07:00","id":1411079,"title":"","content":"In my game, the Great Recession of 2007 was a Paradox backlash against the Syndicate, who tried to win it all. Their failure opened the door to the other Conventions scape-goating them for all manner of unrelated problems (like the issues the Progenitors have in AkatsukiLeader13's post). The Syndicate has been put on a very tight leash, but their subtle forms of pushback have created or expanded rifts throughout the Technocracy. A little financial manipulation goes a long way. Fractures between and within the Conventions mean that everyone will be looking for an edge. In game, that might translate into the formation of brief alliances with Tradition mages in order to strike against enemies in ways they wouldn't expect. All the better if you can convince your allies of the moment that your opponents are corrupted by the Nephandi. And even better if you're the one already corrupted!<br /> <br /> I do prefer the idea that the Technocracy and Traditions can team up against significant threats. The Ascension War is still ongoing, and there are factions within the Conventions that will happily wreck or capture Tradition mages when they can, but overwhelming threats require uneasy alliances. One could also argue that the Technocracy now views the Traditions as barely worth their attention, pathetic throwbacks who long ago made their last stamp on world progress. In my chronicle, the Traditions took advantage of Technocratic arrogance and division and staged a bit of a comeback. Now the world is facing its potential end point due to a confluence of significant threats, and some degree of alliance is desperately needed...but not yet in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}